or_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":76,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["express","expressjs","fast","fiber","flexible","framework","friendly","go","golang","hacktoberfest","hacktoberfest2020","nodejs","performance","rest-api","web"],"visibility":"public","forks":1923,"open_issues":76,"watchers":38715,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gofiber/fiber/pulls/580","html_url":"https://github.com/gofiber/fiber/pull/580","diff_url":"https://github.com/gofiber/fiber/pull/580.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/gofiber/fiber/pull/580.patch","merged_at":"2020-07-12T00:35:13Z"},"body":"Currently, `Fiber` uses `utils.GetArgument(flagChild)` to determine whether the current process is a child process from prefork. According to #522 and #469, we know that users have some side effects when using `flag.Parse()`.\r\n\r\nMy current approach is to use environment variables to determine whether the current process is a child process. When spawning a child process, add `FIBER_PREFORK_CHILD=1` environment variable for inter-process communication. This has several advantages:\r\n- No longer affects anything related to the flag, so there is no need for the hijacking code added in #542 (some are copied from the standard library)\r\n- `FIBER_PREFORK_CHILD` this environment variable is basically impossible to conflict with the user’s environment variables\r\n\r\nAs for the global variable names that control environment variables, I use `envPreforkChildKey` and `envPreforkChildVal`, if you think there are better variable names, I will replace them.\r\n\r\nFinally, I was thinking about whether I need to add an environment variable, which has the same effect as `settings.Prefork`, for .e.g\r\n```go\r\n\tif app.Settings.Prefork || os.Getenv(\"FIBER_PREFORK\") == \"1\"{\r\n\t\treturn app.prefork(addr, tlsconfig...)\r\n\t}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf this is the case, I also need to pass the `FIBER_PREFORK` environment variable to the child process.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gofiber/fiber/issues/580/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gofiber/fiber/issues/580/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]